Subject: Backtraces decide the compiled-record scan once

What this does
  regvm_fill_backtrace_frames sets rec_scan (QJS_RECSCAN or form bit 2) the first time it runs, as regvm_merge_fl_records already did, and then tests the cached value.

Why we need it
  Until the merge ran, rec_scan stayed unset and every backtrace called getenv("QJS_RECSCAN"): 3.4% of the instructions of kit throws (one backtrace per thrown error), which went from 3273.0 to 3807.7 M compiled instructions in the green run.

Soundness
  The value is the one the merge computes: the form bits come from the units' constructors, which run before any code, and the environment variable is read once as before.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index cc3c961..3b970f8 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -31939 +31939,5 @@ static int regvm_fill_backtrace_frames(JSRuntime *rt, JSRegBtFrame *bt, int max)
-    if ((qjs_aot_form_v & 4) || rt->aot_fl_top != NULL || rec_scan > 0 || (rec_scan < 0 && ((qjs_aot_form_v & 2) || getenv("QJS_RECSCAN"))))
+    /* rec_scan is decided once (the form bits are set by the units' constructors, before any code runs): an unset QJS_RECSCAN was
+       looked up again on every backtrace. */
+    if (rec_scan < 0)
+        rec_scan = (qjs_aot_form_v & 2) || getenv("QJS_RECSCAN") != NULL;
+    if ((qjs_aot_form_v & 4) || rt->aot_fl_top != NULL || rec_scan > 0)
